Shadows: read shadow atlas depth with a nearest sampler

The soft-shadow blocker search and the transmittance depth reads sample
the positional and directional shadow atlases through
SAMPLER_LINEAR_CLAMP without depth compare. The atlases are D16_UNORM
or D32_SFLOAT, and linear filtering of depth formats is optional in
Vulkan. On a device without it, the validation layer reports
VUID-vkCmdDrawIndexed-magFilter-04553 for every scene draw and the
depth read is undefined.

These reads want a stored depth, not a blend: the blocker search tests
each tap against the receiver depth, and a linear blend across a
silhouette edge yields a depth no occluder has. Use
SAMPLER_NEAREST_CLAMP for them. PCF lookups keep the compare sampler.

Not covered: volumetric_fog_process.glsl (Forward+ only) reads the
atlases through its own linear_sampler binding.

Applied by godot/CMakeLists.txt on top of GODOT_GIT_REF, after 0004.

